# Issue #104: undirected flows (<-> and --) are followed from either
# end, as they are for neighbors, so bc and bd are path flows and stay;
# ca (C -> A) is off the upstream paths from D and is hidden.

process A
process B
process C
process D

A -> B ab
B <-> C bc
C -> D cd
B -- D bd
C -> A ca

!!<2 D
